{{Culture of Hong Kong}}
{{History of art sidebar}}
The '''visual art of Hong Kong''', or '''Hong Kong art''', refers to all forms of [[Visual arts|visual art]] in or associated with [[Hong Kong]] throughout its history and towards the present. The history of Hong Kong art is closely related to the broader history of [[Chinese art]], alongside the [[Taiwanese art|art of Taiwan]] and [[Culture of Macau|Macau]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal |last=Clarke |first=David |date=2000 |title=The Culture of a Border Within: Hong Kong Art and China |journal=Art Journal |volume=59 |issue=2 |pages=88–101|doi=10.1080/00043249.2000.10791999 |s2cid=191995533 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite book |last=Clarke |first=David J. |title=Art & place : essays on art from a Hong Kong perspective |date=1996 |publisher=Hong Kong University Press |isbn=978-988-220-008-1 |location=Hong Kong |oclc=672434491}}</ref> Hong Kong art may include pottery and rock art from Hong Kong's prehistoric periods; calligraphy, Chinese ink painting, and pottery from its time under Imperial China; paintings from the New Ink Painting Movement and avant-garde art emerging during Hong Kong's colonial period; and the [[contemporary art]] practices in post-handover Hong Kong today.

The consciousness of [[modern art]] and international art movements may be observed in Hong Kong in the late 1960s and early 1970s.<ref name=":0" /> The emergence of the New Ink Painting Movement during that period saw aspects of [[Ink wash painting|Chinese ink painting]] incorporated with the gestural brushwork of [[Abstract expressionism|Abstract Expressionism]].<ref name=":0" />

Hong Kong is now considered a significant regional art market due to its unique historical development and geographical position.<ref name=":3">{{Cite web |last=Lin |first=Kurt |date=28 March 2019 |title=Hong Kong: welcome to the epicentre for the arts trade |url=http://multimedia.scmp.com/native/infographics/article/3002336/how-has-hong-kong-come/ |access-date=2023-01-16 |website=South China Morning Post |language=en}}</ref>

