{{Popular music}}

This article outlines trends in '''[[popular music]]''' during the 2020s. The early years of the decade were particularly challenging for the music industry, as the [[COVID-19 pandemic]] forced widespread concert cancellations and disrupted traditional live performances. In response, video platforms like [[TikTok]] quickly rose to prominence, becoming key tastemakers and driving musical trends by launching [[Viral marketing|viral hits]]. By mid-2023, the industry recorded its highest annual revenue to date ($8.4 billion), partly due to the growth of streaming subscriptions.

