'''''National Treasure: Edge of History''''' is an American [[Action (fiction)|action]]-[[Adventure (genre)|adventure]] television series developed for and globally released on the streaming service [[Disney+]]. It is based on, and a continuation of, the [[National Treasure (franchise)|''National Treasure'' franchise]]. It was produced by [[Jerry Bruckheimer Films#Television|Jerry Bruckheimer Television]] and [[ABC Signature]].<ref name="TVseries_TV">{{Cite web |last=Peters |first=Jay |date=May 8, 2020 |title=A National Treasure Disney Plus series is in development |url=https://www.theverge.com/2020/5/7/21251444/national-treasure-disney-plus-series-development-theatrical-movie-3 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200601082712/https://www.theverge.com/2020/5/7/21251444/national-treasure-disney-plus-series-development-theatrical-movie-3 |archive-date=June 1, 2020 |access-date=July 4, 2020 |website=[[The Verge]]}}</ref> The series stars [[Lisette Olivera]], with [[Catherine Zeta-Jones]] as the apparent lead antagonist, and with [[Justin Bartha]] reprising his role from the films as a recurring character, while [[Harvey Keitel]] appears in the beginning, also reprising his film role. [[Mira Nair]] directed the pilot episode. The show primarily filmed in [[Baton Rouge, Louisiana]], and [[Santa Fe, New Mexico]], and premiered on December 14, 2022.<ref name="SeriesPremiere">{{Cite web |last=Schwartz |first=Ryan |date=September 10, 2022 |title=''National Treasure'' Sequel Series Trailer Features Nod to MIA Nicolas Cage — Gets Disney+ Premiere Date |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/national-treasure-sequel-release-date-cast-returning-disney-plus-tv-series-1234853446/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220910230207/https://tvline.com/2022/09/10/national-treasure-sequel-release-date-cast-returning-disney-plus-tv-series/ |archive-date=September 10, 2022 |access-date=September 10, 2022 |work=[[TVLine]]}}</ref>

''National Treasure: Edge of History'' received generally mixed reviews from critics. It was among the ten most-streamed original programs in the U.S. from its first week, before it reached the top 5 in its later weeks. In April 2023, the series was canceled after one season.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Romano |first=Nick |date=April 21, 2023 |title='National Treasure' series canceled at Disney+ after 1 season |url=https://ew.com/tv/national-treasure-series-canceled-disney-plus/ |access-date=2023-08-25 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |language=en}}</ref>

